@startuml uc_kafka_eventing
' Cas d'utilisation — Kafka & Eventing côté client
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #F7F9FC
  BorderColor #2C3E50
}
skinparam actorStyle awesome
left to right direction

actor "MEMBER" as MEMBER
actor "CLIENT_ADMIN" as CADMIN
actor "ADMIN" as ADMIN
actor "Kafka (Strimzi)" as KAFKA <<système>>
actor "Knative Eventing" as KNE <<système>>

rectangle "Kafka & Eventing" {

  package "Topics (/api/kafka/topics)" {
    usecase "Créer un topic\n(name, partitions, replicas, config)" as UC_TCREATE
    usecase "Lister ses topics" as UC_TLIST
    usecase "Consulter un topic" as UC_TGET
    usecase "Supprimer un topic" as UC_TDEL
  }

  package "Eventing (/api/eventing)" {
    usecase "Créer un KafkaSource" as UC_SCREATE
    usecase "Lister ses KafkaSources\n(+ état ready réel)" as UC_SLIST
    usecase "Créer un Trigger\n(filtre sur le type d'événement)" as UC_TRCREATE
    usecase "Lister ses Triggers" as UC_TRLIST
    usecase "Supprimer un Trigger" as UC_TRDEL
  }

  usecase "Publier un CloudEvent\nPOST /api/events" as UC_PUB

  usecase "Garantir l'existence du Broker 'default'\ndans le namespace tenant" as UC_BROKER
  usecase "Créer le topic dans Kafka\n(AdminClient.createTopics)" as UC_KTOPIC
  usecase "Câbler automatiquement\nKafkaSource + Trigger au déploiement" as UC_AUTO
  usecase "Supprimer en cascade les CR d'eventing\nlors de la suppression d'une app" as UC_CASCADE

  usecase "Lister tous les topics de la plateforme\nGET /api/admin/kafka/topics" as UC_ATLIST
  usecase "Forcer la suppression d'un topic\nDELETE /api/admin/kafka/topics/{id}" as UC_ATDEL
}

MEMBER --> UC_TCREATE
MEMBER --> UC_TLIST
MEMBER --> UC_TGET
MEMBER --> UC_TDEL
MEMBER --> UC_SCREATE
MEMBER --> UC_SLIST
MEMBER --> UC_TRCREATE
MEMBER --> UC_TRLIST
MEMBER --> UC_TRDEL
MEMBER --> UC_PUB
CADMIN --|> MEMBER
ADMIN  --> UC_ATLIST
ADMIN  --> UC_ATDEL

UC_TCREATE  ..> UC_KTOPIC : <<include>>
UC_SCREATE  ..> UC_BROKER : <<include>>
UC_AUTO     ..> UC_SCREATE : <<include>>
UC_AUTO     ..> UC_TRCREATE : <<include>>
UC_PUB      ..> KAFKA : <<include>> KafkaProducer.send()
UC_KTOPIC   ..> KAFKA
UC_SCREATE  ..> KNE
UC_TRCREATE ..> KNE
UC_CASCADE  ..> UC_TRDEL : <<include>>

note bottom of UC_TCREATE
  Permission MANAGE_KAFKA.
  Double contrôle d'unicité :
  existsByNameAndUserId puis existsByName
  (les noms de topics sont uniques cluster-wide).
end note

note bottom of UC_SCREATE
  Permission MANAGE_EVENTING.
  Lecture (GET /sources, /triggers) sans
  permission spécifique : JWT valide suffisant.
end note

' Classes utilisées : KafkaTopic, KafkaTopicDto, CreateTopicRequest, KafkaSource, KafkaSourceDto, Trigger, TriggerDto
' Contrôleurs utilisés : KafkaController, EventingController, EventController, AdminController
' Services utilisés : KafkaService, EventingService, EventService, PermissionService, UserContextService
' Pourquoi ces éléments apparaissent : chaque cas correspond à une méthode de KafkaController/EventingController/EventController ; les cas « système » traduisent ensureBrokerExists(), createTopicInKafka() et deleteByServiceName().
' Fichiers sources vérifiés :
'   kafka/KafkaController.java:19-56 (@PreAuthorize MANAGE_KAFKA sur POST et DELETE uniquement)
'   kafka/KafkaService.java:36-99 (createTopic, listTopics, getTopic, deleteTopic, createTopicInKafka)
'   eventing/EventingController.java:32-84 (@PreAuthorize MANAGE_EVENTING sur POST/DELETE)
'   eventing/EventingService.java:82,113,198,232,270,309,390,398
'   eventing/EventController.java:15-25 ; eventing/EventService.java:26-54
'   app/AppDeploymentAsyncRunner.java:48-63 (câblage automatique)
'   app/AppService.java:178 (eventingService.deleteByServiceName lors du delete)
'   admin/AdminController.java:118-134
' Divergences relevées :
'   - Les topics ne sont PAS créés via la CRD Strimzi « kafka.strimzi.io/KafkaTopic » (pourtant autorisée dans k8s/backend/rbac.yaml:75) mais via l'AdminClient Kafka natif (KafkaService.java:206-217).
'   - Les endpoints de lecture (GET topics, GET sources, GET triggers) ne portent pas d'annotation @PreAuthorize — la permission MANAGE_KAFKA / MANAGE_EVENTING n'est exigée qu'en écriture.
@enduml
